# ATMOS: an atmospheric phase screen applied once at an element (r0 0.25, wavelength 1e-6 base units, tilt
# participation 1, the RAY grid) at the entrance pupil of the manual's Cassegrain, then OPD; and DMBUILD (= BUILD
# in this version) after cutting nGridpts to 21 (cmdref: Source & Wavelength / Linear Model).  The screen takes
# the OPD away from 1.29e-12.  Measured 2026-10-17 (PLAN_CONSOLIDATION 1.2 (p)): the screen is RANDOM and not
# under SEED -- three runs of this journal gave 2.88e-5, 1.36e-5 and, once on ifx, every ray lost at element 4
# ("All rays are obscured or lost", OPD 9.9999e36); the same screen at element 3 (the secondary, a Reflector) lost
# every ray each time.  So this journal pins the dialog and that the OPD changed, not a value.
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
none
opd 5
atm
1
0.25
1e-6
1.0
ray
opd 5
mod nGridpts=21
q
dmbuild
5
# EXPECT: RMS OPD error is\s+1\.293791606D-12[\s\S]*?Enter atmosphere r0: \[0\.250000\]: 0\.25[\s\S]*?Use RAY grid or separate ATMospheric grid\? \[RAY\]: ray[\s\S]*?RMS OPD error is\s+(?!1\.293791606D-12)\d\.\d+D[+-]\d\d
# EXPECT: Tracing\s+277 rays and BUILDing linear model
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
